#!/usr/bin/env bash
set -euo pipefail

mode=${1:-quick}
case "$mode" in
  quick|-h|--help) [[ $# -le 1 ]] || { printf 'usage: pi help [all]\n' >&2; exit 2; } ;;
  all|--all) [[ $# -eq 1 ]] || { printf 'usage: pi help [all]\n' >&2; exit 2; } ;;
  *) printf 'usage: pi help [all]\n' >&2; exit 2 ;;
esac

show_quick() {
  cat <<'HELP'
Pi commands
===========

Remember these three:
  pi                         Work on the repository in the current directory.
  pi-start all               Start the personal surface: desktop tmux (default).
  pi-restart                 Rebuild the personal surface as desktop tmux.

The complete start matrix (flags are per invocation, not persisted):
  pi-start all                         desktop + tmux
  pi-start all -mobile                 mobile  + tmux
  pi-start all -herdr                  desktop + Herdr
  pi-start all -mobile -herdr          mobile  + Herdr

`all` always starts the personal surface. `--mobile` and `--herdr` are
accepted aliases. If the managed grid is already in another matrix cell,
`pi-start all` rebuilds it safely. `pi-restart` forces a clean rebuild.

Choose one destination instead:
  pi-start                   Personal only, desktop tmux.
  pi-start project [DIR]     Project workspace with Neovim + Pi.
  pi-start host              Explicit unsandboxed host-maintenance conversation.

More help:
  pi help all                Full launcher, recovery, and navigation reference.
  pi --help                  Upstream Pi CLI options.
  pidev --help               Project workspace options.
HELP
}

show_all() {
  show_quick
  cat <<'HELP'

Full workspace reference
========================

Backend and layout:
  - Desktop and tmux are defaults on every invocation.
  - `-mobile` changes layout for that invocation only.
  - `-herdr` puts the managed personal surface in Herdr for that invocation only.
  - `pi-start all` safely rebuilds a proven managed grid when its backend or
    layout differs; single-surface starts never replace another live owner.
  - `pi-restart` forces a clean rebuild using the requested matrix cell.
  - Conversation identities survive either backend and layout.

What the layouts contain:
  tmux desktop               Personal roles use paired side-by-side panes.
  tmux mobile                Each conversation gets its own tmux window.
  Herdr desktop              Named session `pi-personal`;
                             personal roles are paired in two Spaces.
  Herdr mobile               The same named session; each personal role gets
                             its own Space.

Start and switch examples:
  pi-start all -mobile       Start or switch the personal surface to mobile tmux.
  pi-start all -herdr        Start or switch the personal surface to desktop Herdr.
  pi-restart -herdr          Force a clean rebuild as desktop Herdr.
  pi-restart -mobile -herdr  Switch cleanly to mobile Herdr.
  pi-restart -mobile         Switch cleanly to mobile tmux.
  pi-restart --no-attach     Rebuild without opening a client.

Other launchers:
  cd REPOSITORY && pi        Start/resume a policy-controlled root conversation.
  cd REPOSITORY && pidev     Neovim on the left and Pi on the right.
  cd REPOSITORY && pidev -mobile
                             Pi only in a full-width project window.
  pi-host                    Resume the single-writer unsandboxed host session for $PWD.

Switch and navigate:
  Ctrl-a p                   Switch to pi-personal in tmux.
  Ctrl-a \                    Toggle the previous tmux session.
  tmux ls                    List tmux sessions.
  tmux attach -t NAME        Attach to a named tmux session.
  Ctrl-b w                   Herdr Spaces/workspace picker.
  Ctrl-b h/j/k/l             Move between Herdr panes.
  Ctrl-b c / n / p           Create, next, or previous Herdr tab.
  Ctrl-b b / q / ?           Sidebar, detach, or Herdr help.

Useful commands inside Pi:
  /goal <objective>          Work continuously toward an objective.
  /goal status|pause|resume  Inspect or control the active goal.
  /goal clear                Remove the active goal.
  /goal --tokens 100k ...    Give a goal an explicit provider-token budget.
  /fast on|off|status        OpenAI priority service is on by default; toggle it here.
  /subagents-fleet           Inspect private child runs.
  /subagents-doctor          Diagnose subagent discovery and routing.
  /observe or Ctrl-I         Inspect task, fleet, messages, and failures.
  Ctrl-g                     Browse conversation history.
  Enter / Alt-Enter          Steer now / queue a follow-up while Pi is busy.

Other tools:
  pi-harness-feedback        Review the central normalized feedback feed.
  pi-harness-feedback --repository PATH
                             Filter harness feedback to one project.

Recovery and maintenance:
  pi-restart                 Rebuild the personal surface as desktop tmux.
  pi-personal --ensure       Repair missing desktop tmux personal panes.
  pi-personal -mobile --ensure
                             Repair mobile tmux personal windows.
  pi-root-session migrate --dry-run
                             Inspect legacy root-session migration.
  pi-root-session migrate    Apply the reviewed root-session migration.
  pi-root-session cleanup --repository PATH
                             Review stale managed worktrees before cleanup.
  pi-sandbox-gc              Inspect stale Pi-owned containers and caches.
  pi-sandbox-gc --apply      Apply only the printed Pi-owned cleanup plan.
  pi-harness-feedback --format markdown --include-reviewed
                             Show reviewed and pending self-improvement feedback.

Safety boundary:
  root, personal             Conversation roles and authority profiles.
  tmux, Herdr                Terminal backends, not authority profiles.
  Only one backend may own a durable managed conversation at a time.
  Ordinary `pi` owns repository trust and sandbox selection. Use `pi-host`
  only when unsandboxed host-user access is intentional.

Compatibility aliases:
  pi --help-custom           Same as `pi help`.
  pi-start help              Same quick guide.
HELP
}

if [[ "$mode" == all || "$mode" == --all ]]; then show_all; else show_quick; fi
